  "description": "Waterlogged blocks as water sources: stairs, bottom and top slabs, a fence, leaves, scaffolding, closed and open trapdoors, a chest, a lantern, iron bars, a wall, a chain, a sign, a copper grate and a rail placed waterlogged, each in a walled basin; once a neighbour changes, the water flows out through the faces their shapes leave open (canPassThroughWall), and dries up when they are dry again. Flowing water does not enter dry waterloggable blocks.",
